WEBVTT

00:00:02.002 --> 00:00:02.969
New man coming!

00:00:03.036 --> 00:00:05.197
New prisoner!
Get out of my way!

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:06.762
New man coming!

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:08.296
Get out of my way!

00:00:09.909 --> 00:00:12.469
Here he comes!
Get ready! Let's go!

00:00:12.512 --> 00:00:13.536
Hurry up!

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:14.604
They're gonna push off!
Let's go!

00:00:14.647 --> 00:00:15.614
New prisoner!

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:18.276
Hey!
Something's coming down there!

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:39.035
Hey, get out of my...

00:01:09.536 --> 00:01:10.730
Kill him! Kill him!

00:01:16.376 --> 00:01:17.570
Tom!

00:03:26.270 --> 00:03:28.261
Nobody touch him.
He's mine.

00:03:38.149 --> 00:03:41.607
Wait. This is a mistake.

00:03:41.652 --> 00:03:42.880
I don't belong here!

00:03:42.920 --> 00:03:44.979
You don't?

00:03:45.022 --> 00:03:47.513
Well, I'll just take
you home, then.

00:03:47.558 --> 00:03:49.082
All right?!

00:03:53.130 --> 00:03:55.462
This one's mine.

00:03:55.499 --> 00:03:57.831
I say he's not.

00:03:57.868 --> 00:04:01.201
He's the reason that I'm here.

00:04:01.238 --> 00:04:04.901
He was my partner in a bombing.

00:04:04.942 --> 00:04:09.140
We killed 47 patrollers
on Akritiri... 47!

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:12.809
And then this scum
confessed to the tribunal

00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:14.374
and gave them my name.

00:04:14.418 --> 00:04:15.942
So I'm telling you again,

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:17.647
he's mine.

00:04:19.090 --> 00:04:20.955
I'm keeping him.

00:04:27.064 --> 00:04:29.055
Take him.

00:04:32.169 --> 00:04:33.966
For now.

00:04:52.590 --> 00:04:55.081
Did you have to hit me so hard?

00:04:55.126 --> 00:04:56.684
Trust me... around here

00:04:56.727 --> 00:04:59.195
you don't want anybody
thinking you're soft.

00:04:59.230 --> 00:05:00.527
Thanks for the tip.

00:05:00.564 --> 00:05:01.826
Is there any food?

00:05:01.866 --> 00:05:04.835
I haven't had anything
to eat since I got here.

00:05:04.869 --> 00:05:05.927
How long is that?

00:05:06.003 --> 00:05:08.164
A couple of days.

00:05:08.205 --> 00:05:10.366
Some shore leave, huh?

00:05:10.407 --> 00:05:13.137
What happened to you
after they split us up?

00:05:13.177 --> 00:05:17.511
The Akritirians interrogated me.

00:05:17.548 --> 00:05:19.641
When I wouldn't confess
to the bombing,

00:05:19.683 --> 00:05:22.481
they dragged me
in front of a judge.

00:05:22.520 --> 00:05:25.455
He said you'd already
confessed for the both of us

00:05:25.489 --> 00:05:27.320
and then
he pronounced me guilty.

00:05:27.358 --> 00:05:28.950
That's exactly
what happened to me.

00:05:29.026 --> 00:05:32.518
Then they must have drugged me
because the next thing I knew,

00:05:32.563 --> 00:05:34.758
I woke up
at the bottom of the chute

00:05:34.798 --> 00:05:36.095
to that welcoming party.

00:05:36.133 --> 00:05:40.695
We've got to explain to somebody
that there's been a mistake.

00:05:40.738 --> 00:05:42.968
Who did you have in mind?

00:05:43.007 --> 00:05:44.304
A guard.

00:05:44.341 --> 00:05:45.535
The warden.

00:05:45.576 --> 00:05:48.409
I haven't seen
anybody like that.

00:05:48.445 --> 00:05:50.572
A prison without guards?

00:05:50.614 --> 00:05:53.242
The other inmates say

00:05:53.284 --> 00:05:55.752
this place
is 300 meters underground.

00:05:55.786 --> 00:05:59.745
Maybe the Akritirians figure
guards aren't necessary.

00:05:59.790 --> 00:06:01.417
Can I have some more?

00:06:01.458 --> 00:06:03.255
What do you think this is?!

00:06:03.294 --> 00:06:04.921
A hotel?!
There isn't any more!

00:06:04.995 --> 00:06:07.293
Take it easy!

00:06:14.305 --> 00:06:16.830
I'm sorry.

00:06:16.874 --> 00:06:20.708
I'm...
really starting to get edgy.

00:06:20.744 --> 00:06:22.735
I think it's the clamp.

00:06:22.780 --> 00:06:23.872
The what?

00:06:27.084 --> 00:06:29.644
That's what the prisoners
call it.

00:06:29.687 --> 00:06:31.154
Everybody has one.

00:06:32.723 --> 00:06:34.520
What is it?

00:06:34.558 --> 00:06:38.358
I'm guessing it's some kind
of synaptic stimulator.

00:06:38.395 --> 00:06:41.489
Anyway, it's affecting
my nervous system.

00:06:41.532 --> 00:06:44.194
I've been getting jumpier
ever since I got here.

00:06:44.235 --> 00:06:47.261
Not to mention,
this thing itches like crazy.

00:06:47.304 --> 00:06:48.396
What do you think it's for?

00:06:48.439 --> 00:06:51.237
Maybe it's some kind
of torture device.

00:06:51.275 --> 00:06:53.300
We could try taking them out.

00:06:53.344 --> 00:06:55.244
No! I saw someone try it.

00:06:55.279 --> 00:06:56.940
It killed him.

00:07:02.286 --> 00:07:07.451
What we have to do
is find a way out of this place.

00:07:08.993 --> 00:07:10.119
Hmm.

00:07:12.496 --> 00:07:14.726
Let's get something
straight first.

00:07:14.765 --> 00:07:16.858
What?

00:07:16.900 --> 00:07:20.199
The next time you take
a swing at me,

00:07:20.237 --> 00:07:22.171
I'm hitting back.

00:07:26.176 --> 00:07:27.666
What's that?

00:07:27.711 --> 00:07:30.373
Another prisoner, maybe?

00:07:30.414 --> 00:07:32.644
Food coming!

00:07:32.683 --> 00:07:34.241
- Food!
- Join me for dinner?

00:07:51.935 --> 00:07:53.630
No! There's got to be more!

00:08:04.281 --> 00:08:06.408
I don't think he was going
to eat it anyway, do you?

00:08:12.656 --> 00:08:14.214
He's dead.

00:08:15.526 --> 00:08:18.723
I think I've lost my appetite.

00:08:24.435 --> 00:08:28.269
Captain's Log, Stardate 50156.2.

00:08:28.305 --> 00:08:29.932
After 72 hours,
Lieutenant Paris

00:08:30.007 --> 00:08:31.941
and Ensign Kim
are still missing,

00:08:32.042 --> 00:08:33.703
and I'm quickly losing patience

00:08:33.744 --> 00:08:35.575
with the Akritirian authorities.

00:08:35.612 --> 00:08:37.512
They continue to deny us
access to the surface,

00:08:37.548 --> 00:08:39.345
and they've yet to confirm

00:08:39.383 --> 00:08:42.079
whether our crewmen
were killed in the bombing.

00:08:42.119 --> 00:08:43.518
Anything?

00:08:43.554 --> 00:08:45.852
I have completed another
full sensor sweep

00:08:45.889 --> 00:08:48.119
including a multispectral
subsurface scan.

00:08:48.158 --> 00:08:49.750
I still cannot locate
their life signs

00:08:49.793 --> 00:08:51.317
or their combadges.

00:08:51.362 --> 00:08:55.059
Captain, Ambassador Liria
is hailing us.

00:08:55.099 --> 00:08:57.294
On screen.

00:08:57.334 --> 00:09:00.201
I'm only in the mood
for good news today, Ambassador.

00:09:00.237 --> 00:09:02.296
I'm afraid I can't oblige.

00:09:02.339 --> 00:09:04.273
Are you saying they're dead?

00:09:04.308 --> 00:09:06.538
No, they're very much alive.

00:09:06.577 --> 00:09:09.137
Then where are they?

00:09:09.179 --> 00:09:12.444
Your men have been convicted
of the terrorist bombing

00:09:12.483 --> 00:09:15.418
at the Laktivia recreational
facility, which resulted

00:09:15.452 --> 00:09:18.717
in the death of 47
off-duty patrollers.

00:09:19.723 --> 00:09:21.190
I assure you, Ambassador,

00:09:21.225 --> 00:09:23.750
my people had nothing to do
with this attack.

00:09:23.794 --> 00:09:25.318
We found chemical traces

00:09:25.362 --> 00:09:27.387
of the explosive used
in the bombing

00:09:27.431 --> 00:09:29.558
on their hands and clothing.

00:09:29.600 --> 00:09:30.794
I'm sure the same could be said

00:09:30.834 --> 00:09:32.461
of anyone who was near
the explosion.

00:09:32.503 --> 00:09:34.437
It's hardly enough evidence
for a conviction.

00:09:34.471 --> 00:09:38.066
The explosive
was trilithium based.

00:09:38.108 --> 00:09:41.339
There is no source of trilithium
anywhere in our system.

00:09:41.378 --> 00:09:45.940
So, you can imagine our surprise
when our investigation revealed

00:09:46.049 --> 00:09:48.711
that your ship is powered
by dilithium...

00:09:48.752 --> 00:09:54.384
which our scientists tell us is
convertible into trilithium.

00:09:54.425 --> 00:09:56.325
We have long suspected

00:09:56.360 --> 00:09:58.624
that the so-called
Open Sky terrorists

00:09:58.662 --> 00:10:01.597
had off-world collaborators.

00:10:01.632 --> 00:10:03.964
Now we know who they are.

00:10:04.001 --> 00:10:07.232
Captain, two Akritirian ships
are approaching

00:10:07.271 --> 00:10:09.330
at bearing 271 mark 64.

00:10:09.373 --> 00:10:12.672
Prepare your ship
for inspection, Captain.

00:10:12.709 --> 00:10:15.405
If it will help confirm
our innocence, I'll consider it.

00:10:15.446 --> 00:10:18.210
But first, I want to know
where my people are being held,

00:10:18.248 --> 00:10:20.148
and I want to talk
to them immediately.

00:10:20.184 --> 00:10:22.982
Communication with inmates
is not permitted.

00:10:23.020 --> 00:10:24.988
If you want my cooperation,
Ambassador,

00:10:25.022 --> 00:10:27.490
you're going to have
to do better than that.

00:10:27.524 --> 00:10:29.321
Perhaps you've misunderstood me.

00:10:29.359 --> 00:10:31.589
Let me clarify our position.

00:10:31.628 --> 00:10:33.459
Your vessel is being impounded.

00:10:33.497 --> 00:10:35.795
You and your crew
are under arrest.

00:10:35.833 --> 00:10:37.300
Prepare to be boarded.

00:10:37.334 --> 00:10:40.167
Captain, their ships
are powering weapons.

00:10:40.204 --> 00:10:42.195
Mr. Tuvok, raise shields.

00:10:42.239 --> 00:10:44.002
Mr. Chakotay, take the conn.

00:10:44.074 --> 00:10:45.632
I'd like to resolve
this situation

00:10:45.676 --> 00:10:47.007
peacefully, Ambassador,

00:10:47.110 --> 00:10:49.408
but let me clarify my position.

00:10:49.446 --> 00:10:51.971
I will not allow
this ship to be boarded.

00:10:52.015 --> 00:10:56.247
That, Captain,
is an error in judgment.

00:11:04.528 --> 00:11:06.723
Captain, should I return fire?

00:11:06.763 --> 00:11:09.323
That's not going to help us
get Tom and Harry back.

00:11:09.366 --> 00:11:10.333
We need to regroup.

00:11:10.367 --> 00:11:11.766
Get us out of here, Commander.

00:11:11.802 --> 00:11:13.003
Aye, Captain.

00:11:37.427 --> 00:11:38.689
What took you so long?

00:11:38.728 --> 00:11:40.889
I've been back
at least half an hour.

00:11:40.930 --> 00:11:44.889
You're starting to
feel it, aren't you?

00:11:44.934 --> 00:11:46.401
I guess I am.

00:11:46.436 --> 00:11:48.267
It gets worse all the time.

00:11:48.304 --> 00:11:49.771
We have to fight it.

00:11:51.441 --> 00:11:53.602
Let's focus
on something positive.

00:11:55.545 --> 00:11:57.843
How about...

00:11:57.881 --> 00:12:00.509
a seven-course dinner?

00:12:02.218 --> 00:12:04.345
I suppose you didn't
find any food.

00:12:04.387 --> 00:12:07.151
Well... I found close
to 50 good citizens

00:12:07.190 --> 00:12:11.422
in this quaint little community,
but not a grocer among them.

00:12:11.461 --> 00:12:13.258
I take it that's a no.

00:12:13.296 --> 00:12:14.456
Yeah.

00:12:14.497 --> 00:12:17.762
But, if we ever do get
our hands on some food,

00:12:17.801 --> 00:12:20.361
I found a lovely
spot for a picnic.

00:12:20.403 --> 00:12:21.427
Great.

00:12:21.471 --> 00:12:23.962
All we need
are the Delaney sisters,

00:12:24.074 --> 00:12:26.304
and we could make a day of it.

00:12:28.078 --> 00:12:29.136
So, how about you?

00:12:29.179 --> 00:12:32.114
Come across anything interesting
in your travels?

00:12:32.148 --> 00:12:33.672
If you mean an escape route,

00:12:33.716 --> 00:12:35.707
I ran into nothing
but solid walls.

00:12:36.753 --> 00:12:38.448
Me, too.

00:12:38.488 --> 00:12:40.786
As far as I can see,
the only way to the surface

00:12:40.824 --> 00:12:42.553
is that chute
in the main chamber.

00:12:42.592 --> 00:12:44.583
The question is:
How do we get into it

00:12:44.627 --> 00:12:46.993
without getting fried
by that force field?

00:12:47.097 --> 00:12:50.225
You saw what happened
to the man who reached inside.

00:12:50.266 --> 00:12:52.325
That's where this
might come in handy.

00:12:52.368 --> 00:12:55.804
I thought if we could get
our hands on some loose wiring,

00:12:55.839 --> 00:12:57.431
you might be able to use it
to rig a device

00:12:57.474 --> 00:12:59.271
that would short out
the force field

00:12:59.309 --> 00:13:01.072
long enough for us
to get into the tube.

00:13:01.111 --> 00:13:03.477
It's worth a try.

00:13:03.513 --> 00:13:04.946
Yeah.

00:13:05.048 --> 00:13:07.414
Now, if we could only
figure out a way

00:13:07.450 --> 00:13:10.351
to short out these implants,
we'd be all set.

00:13:13.823 --> 00:13:15.723
There's no indication
they followed us.

00:13:15.758 --> 00:13:16.850
I guess they're more interested

00:13:16.893 --> 00:13:18.622
in getting rid of us
than finding out the truth.

00:13:18.661 --> 00:13:19.628
We've got to go back

00:13:19.662 --> 00:13:20.959
- for Harry and Tom.
- B'Elanna...

00:13:21.064 --> 00:13:23.362
We have no information
as to their whereabouts,

00:13:23.399 --> 00:13:24.696
and if we return
to Akritirian space,

00:13:24.734 --> 00:13:26.759
we are sure to encounter
further hostilities.

00:13:26.803 --> 00:13:27.929
Tuvok is right.

00:13:27.971 --> 00:13:30.337
Let's concentrate on proving
Harry and Tom's innocence.

00:13:30.373 --> 00:13:31.670
How do we do that?

00:13:31.708 --> 00:13:33.699
We know the explosive
was trilithium-based.

00:13:33.743 --> 00:13:35.677
If we find the source
of that trilithium,

00:13:35.712 --> 00:13:37.270
it may lead us
to the real bombers.

00:13:37.313 --> 00:13:39.281
Our long-range scans indicate
that Liria was right.

00:13:39.315 --> 00:13:41.180
There's no trilithium
in this sector.

00:13:41.217 --> 00:13:43.310
What about paralithium?

00:13:44.320 --> 00:13:45.309
It's used as a fuel

00:13:45.355 --> 00:13:47.289
for some ion-based
propulsion systems

00:13:47.323 --> 00:13:49.621
and it can be converted
into trilithium.

00:13:49.659 --> 00:13:50.990
Review our sensor logs

00:13:51.027 --> 00:13:53.791
of ships entering and leaving
Akritirian space

00:13:53.830 --> 00:13:55.798
during the time
we were in orbit.

00:13:55.832 --> 00:13:58.164
If anybody's using
paralithium for fuel,

00:13:58.201 --> 00:14:01.295
I want to find out who they are
and where they went.

00:14:05.875 --> 00:14:08.844
Come on, come on, come on...

00:14:08.878 --> 00:14:10.937
Take it easy.

00:14:11.047 --> 00:14:12.708
You'll get it.

00:14:23.393 --> 00:14:26.453
I can't think.
I can't concentrate.

00:14:26.496 --> 00:14:29.363
Okay, okay, concentrate on this.

00:14:29.399 --> 00:14:32.527
Uh... um...

00:14:32.569 --> 00:14:34.503
crown roast of lamb

00:14:34.537 --> 00:14:37.529
with, uh... a bed of wild rice

00:14:37.574 --> 00:14:41.533
and a 2296 Chateau
Lafite Rothschild...

00:14:41.578 --> 00:14:44.911
at the real Sandrine's.

00:14:46.249 --> 00:14:50.083
Or how about shrimp
with fettran sauce,

00:14:50.119 --> 00:14:51.814
flambé noodles...

00:14:51.854 --> 00:14:56.154
and fudge ripple pudding.

00:14:56.192 --> 00:14:58.160
Good one.

00:14:58.194 --> 00:14:59.252
Okay. Uh...

00:14:59.295 --> 00:15:02.560
couple of barbecued
T-bone steaks

00:15:02.599 --> 00:15:04.829
with baked Risan beans

00:15:04.867 --> 00:15:07.836
and... cherry pie for dessert.

00:15:07.870 --> 00:15:09.929
Let's see you top that one.

00:15:10.039 --> 00:15:11.597
Right now, I'm so hungry,

00:15:11.641 --> 00:15:14.838
I could eat a bowl of
Neelix's leola root stew.

00:15:14.877 --> 00:15:16.504
Me, too.

00:15:16.546 --> 00:15:19.674
Never thought I'd say that.

00:15:19.716 --> 00:15:22.048
I'm ready to give it a try.

00:15:24.220 --> 00:15:26.552
So far, so good.

00:15:31.361 --> 00:15:33.056
Are you okay?

00:15:35.064 --> 00:15:37.191
What are you doing?

00:15:37.233 --> 00:15:39.394
Just out for a little stroll.

00:15:40.570 --> 00:15:42.060
Move it!

00:15:43.072 --> 00:15:44.972
What's that?

00:15:45.074 --> 00:15:46.974
A pipe.

00:15:47.076 --> 00:15:48.873
Let's see it.

00:15:48.911 --> 00:15:49.935
Come on.

00:15:49.979 --> 00:15:53.540
I'd really recommend
that you stay out of my way.

00:15:53.583 --> 00:15:57.075
You should have thought of that
before you took him!

00:16:08.164 --> 00:16:09.290
Come on, Tom.

00:16:17.473 --> 00:16:18.269
Tom!

00:16:31.721 --> 00:16:37.353
Back off! Back off!
Back off! Back off!

00:16:41.397 --> 00:16:44.958
Hang on. I'm getting
you out of here.

00:16:45.068 --> 00:16:47.730
No fight. No fight.

00:16:50.740 --> 00:16:53.607
If he doesn't bleed to death,
he'll die from infection.

00:16:53.643 --> 00:16:54.974
We've got to get him
to a doctor.

00:16:55.044 --> 00:16:56.671
Of course. We'll call
an emergency vehicle

00:16:56.713 --> 00:16:58.203
and rush him to a hospital.

00:17:09.359 --> 00:17:10.519
Hey!

00:17:12.395 --> 00:17:14.693
What do you want
for the dead man's boots?

00:17:28.578 --> 00:17:30.068
You can make it.

00:17:30.113 --> 00:17:31.205
Just a few more steps,

00:17:31.247 --> 00:17:33.374
and we'll be back
to the shelter.

00:17:33.416 --> 00:17:34.781
Home, sweet home.

00:17:36.953 --> 00:17:38.181
Harry.

00:17:38.221 --> 00:17:39.245
Yeah.

00:17:39.288 --> 00:17:41.586
I'm hurt pretty bad.

00:17:41.624 --> 00:17:43.421
I'll take care of it.

00:17:43.459 --> 00:17:45.586
Promise me something.

00:17:45.628 --> 00:17:47.755
What?

00:17:47.797 --> 00:17:50.095
If things get worse...

00:17:50.133 --> 00:17:53.193
if it comes down
to making a choice,

00:17:53.236 --> 00:17:55.534
don't worry about me.

00:17:55.571 --> 00:17:58.563
Take care of yourself.

00:18:03.246 --> 00:18:04.907
Do we have a deal?

00:18:06.149 --> 00:18:08.481
Quiet.

00:18:09.519 --> 00:18:10.918
Hey!

00:18:10.987 --> 00:18:12.750
What are you doing in there?

00:18:12.789 --> 00:18:14.814
- Get out.
- This place is ours.

00:18:14.857 --> 00:18:17.758
Get out! Get out!
Get out!

00:18:33.443 --> 00:18:35.877
Okay, here's the deal.

00:18:35.912 --> 00:18:38.437
My boots for some clean cloth,

00:18:38.481 --> 00:18:40.813
a liter of water,
two of those food cakes

00:18:40.850 --> 00:18:42.977
and my friend gets to stay
in there until he's better.

00:18:45.121 --> 00:18:47.589
I don't take in boarders.

00:18:47.623 --> 00:18:49.318
What about the rest of it?

00:18:52.395 --> 00:18:53.953
I don't like the color.

00:18:54.063 --> 00:18:56.964
Come on, let's go.

00:18:56.999 --> 00:18:58.557
This guy's not going to help us.

00:19:00.570 --> 00:19:02.094
Just tell me what you want

00:19:02.138 --> 00:19:04.368
for the food
and the bandages, okay?

00:19:05.741 --> 00:19:08.801
That pipe you were working with
interests me.

00:19:08.845 --> 00:19:10.812
I can't trade the pipe.

00:19:10.945 --> 00:19:12.742
Then I guess
we don't have a deal.

00:19:12.780 --> 00:19:15.044
Now move on.
You're blocking my light.

00:19:18.419 --> 00:19:19.716
I'll take you with me.

00:19:19.754 --> 00:19:22.552
Take me where?

00:19:22.590 --> 00:19:25.058
I know a way out of this place.

00:19:25.092 --> 00:19:26.582
I been in here six years.

00:19:26.627 --> 00:19:28.458
I've never heard of a way out.

00:19:28.496 --> 00:19:29.861
The chute.

00:19:31.265 --> 00:19:33.256
Anybody that tries
to get in there

00:19:33.301 --> 00:19:35.132
gets hit with an energy pulse.

00:19:35.169 --> 00:19:37.637
With this pipe,
I can disable the force field.

00:19:37.672 --> 00:19:40.505
With a little luck,
we can make it to the surface.

00:19:49.050 --> 00:19:50.574
What are you staring at?

00:19:50.618 --> 00:19:54.076
I'm trying to figure out
if you're a liar...

00:19:54.121 --> 00:19:56.681
or if the clamp has
already made you crazy.

00:19:56.724 --> 00:19:57.691
Neither.

00:19:57.725 --> 00:19:59.920
And I'll prove it to you.

00:20:01.128 --> 00:20:02.959
You stand your ground.

00:20:03.064 --> 00:20:04.088
I like that.

00:20:04.131 --> 00:20:06.656
Then we have a deal?

00:20:06.701 --> 00:20:09.636
Just remember one thing:

00:20:11.639 --> 00:20:15.439
If you're lying, I'll kill you.

00:20:18.145 --> 00:20:20.170
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:20:20.214 --> 00:20:22.546
So far, we've located
three ships

00:20:22.583 --> 00:20:24.915
with paralithium plasma
emissions,

00:20:24.952 --> 00:20:27.580
but none of them appears
to have produced explosives.

00:20:27.622 --> 00:20:29.920
We're currently in pursuit
of a fourth vessel.

00:20:29.957 --> 00:20:31.356
We're in hailing range

00:20:31.392 --> 00:20:33.292
of the Akritirian
freighter, Captain.

00:20:33.327 --> 00:20:35.454
I'm only reading
two life signs aboard.

00:20:35.496 --> 00:20:36.963
Open a channel.

00:20:36.998 --> 00:20:38.488
This is Kathryn Janeway

00:20:38.532 --> 00:20:40.693
of the Federation
Starship Voyager

00:20:40.735 --> 00:20:43.761
to the Captain
of the Akritirian cargo vessel.

00:20:44.472 --> 00:20:45.496
I'm the Captain of this vessel.

00:20:45.539 --> 00:20:46.665
What do you want?

00:20:46.707 --> 00:20:49.141
Two of my crew members
were convicted

00:20:49.176 --> 00:20:51.542
by the Akritirians
of a terrorist bombing.

00:20:51.579 --> 00:20:53.774
We're trying to prove
their innocence

00:20:53.814 --> 00:20:56.647
and we have reason to believe
a ship like yours,

00:20:56.684 --> 00:21:00.120
which uses paralithium for fuel,
might have been involved

00:21:00.154 --> 00:21:02.315
in the production
of the explosives.

00:21:02.356 --> 00:21:03.755
Let's get out of here.

00:21:03.791 --> 00:21:04.758
Quiet.

00:21:04.792 --> 00:21:06.555
This is a cargo vessel.

00:21:06.594 --> 00:21:08.391
Then you won't mind
if a few of my crew members

00:21:08.429 --> 00:21:09.726
come aboard to have
a look around.

00:21:09.764 --> 00:21:11.823
Not if they don't mind
having their throats cut.

00:21:11.866 --> 00:21:13.595
There's no need to be abrupt...

00:21:17.004 --> 00:21:18.164
I guess you're not
the only captain

00:21:18.205 --> 00:21:19.866
who doesn't want
their ship boarded.

00:21:19.907 --> 00:21:23.968
Captain, I'm picking up
residual traces of trilithium.

00:21:24.011 --> 00:21:26.104
They're faint,
but they're there.

00:21:26.147 --> 00:21:29.548
I think we may have found
our bomb makers.

00:21:29.583 --> 00:21:31.175
Mr. Tuvok, send
a security detail

00:21:31.218 --> 00:21:32.742
to Transporter Room 2.

00:21:32.787 --> 00:21:35.221
Lieutenant Torres,
beam the two of them aboard

00:21:35.256 --> 00:21:37.156
and tractor their ship
into the shuttle bay.

00:21:37.191 --> 00:21:38.920
Aye, Captain.

00:21:44.498 --> 00:21:46.295
You have no right to hold us.

00:21:46.334 --> 00:21:47.699
My people have been accused

00:21:47.735 --> 00:21:50.101
of aiding a terrorist group
called Open Sky.

00:21:50.137 --> 00:21:51.570
What do you know about them?

00:21:51.605 --> 00:21:52.799
They're not terrorists.

00:21:52.840 --> 00:21:53.807
They're patriots.

00:21:53.841 --> 00:21:54.967
One day, they'll lead

00:21:55.009 --> 00:21:57.136
the legitimate government
of our people.

00:21:57.178 --> 00:21:58.304
We don't have

00:21:58.346 --> 00:22:00.473
to answer any
of their questions, Piri.

00:22:00.514 --> 00:22:02.948
It sounds to me
like your young friend here

00:22:02.984 --> 00:22:04.815
sympathizes with these patriots.

00:22:04.852 --> 00:22:05.944
She's not my friend.

00:22:05.987 --> 00:22:07.249
She's my sister.

00:22:07.288 --> 00:22:10.314
And our political views
are none of your business.

00:22:10.358 --> 00:22:13.725
I don't know much
about your world...

00:22:13.761 --> 00:22:14.955
but I do know that my people

00:22:14.996 --> 00:22:16.896
are being held
for a crime they didn't commit

00:22:16.931 --> 00:22:19.456
and I'm going to do everything
in my power to get them out.

00:22:19.500 --> 00:22:20.762
Do you understand that?

00:22:20.801 --> 00:22:22.564
We have confirmed
that explosives

00:22:22.603 --> 00:22:25.595
were indeed produced
aboard their ship.

00:22:25.639 --> 00:22:27.129
Escort them to the brig.

00:22:27.174 --> 00:22:28.607
Aye, Captain.

00:22:28.642 --> 00:22:30.906
And have Mr. Chakotay
lay in a course

00:22:30.945 --> 00:22:32.572
for the Akritirian border.

00:22:32.613 --> 00:22:33.807
Let my sister go.

00:22:33.848 --> 00:22:35.475
She didn't have anything
to do with the bombing,

00:22:35.516 --> 00:22:36.744
and she's only 14.

00:22:36.784 --> 00:22:38.547
Prison doesn't scare me.

00:22:38.586 --> 00:22:39.553
Quiet, Piri.

00:22:39.587 --> 00:22:40.576
Please.

00:22:40.621 --> 00:22:43.112
You don't know
what you're saying.

00:22:43.157 --> 00:22:46.354
Nobody ever gets out
of prison on Akritiri.

00:22:46.394 --> 00:22:48.828
They'll just
let her rot in there

00:22:48.863 --> 00:22:50.694
for the rest of her life.

00:22:50.731 --> 00:22:53.996
I admire your desire
to protect your sister, but...

00:22:54.035 --> 00:22:56.003
it's not really up to me, is it?

00:22:56.070 --> 00:22:57.560
Tell them what we know.

00:22:57.605 --> 00:22:58.697
Tell me what?

00:22:58.739 --> 00:22:59.603
Piri, don't.

00:22:59.640 --> 00:23:01.267
Our brigade found out

00:23:01.308 --> 00:23:05.210
where the maximum security
detention facility is located.

00:23:05.246 --> 00:23:08.044
My sister has quite
a vivid imagination.

00:23:08.082 --> 00:23:10.676
With this ship, you
can attack the prison

00:23:10.718 --> 00:23:12.242
and get your people out.

00:23:12.286 --> 00:23:13.480
I'm sorry,

00:23:13.521 --> 00:23:17.048
that's not how we do things
where I come from.

00:23:17.091 --> 00:23:18.217
Coward.

00:23:21.462 --> 00:23:28.698
Mr. Tuvok, see that they get
a bath and a hot meal.

00:23:36.811 --> 00:23:39.575
I don't trust that guy, Harry.

00:23:39.613 --> 00:23:41.240
I can handle him.

00:23:41.282 --> 00:23:43.773
Just watch your back, okay?

00:23:43.818 --> 00:23:46.286
Try to get some rest.

00:23:46.320 --> 00:23:48.288
Remember our deal?

00:23:48.322 --> 00:23:49.789
What deal?

00:23:49.824 --> 00:23:50.984
If it comes down to it,

00:23:51.025 --> 00:23:53.118
you're going to save
yourself, right?

00:23:54.762 --> 00:23:55.990
If you see a chance,

00:23:56.097 --> 00:23:57.223
just go.

00:23:57.264 --> 00:23:59.459
Don't come back for me.

00:23:59.500 --> 00:24:01.331
I think the clamp

00:24:01.368 --> 00:24:03.928
must really be starting
to make you crazy.

00:24:04.038 --> 00:24:05.266
I'm serious, Harry.

00:24:05.306 --> 00:24:07.604
Getting tired of waiting.

00:24:10.444 --> 00:24:11.570
I gotta go.

00:24:11.612 --> 00:24:13.807
Harry...

00:24:21.789 --> 00:24:23.780
Oh! Damn it!

00:24:23.824 --> 00:24:25.951
Don't fight it, use it.

00:24:27.128 --> 00:24:28.288
How do I do that?

00:24:28.329 --> 00:24:31.890
I feel like there's
a million fire ants in my brain.

00:24:31.932 --> 00:24:34.924
Good. Make them work for you.

00:24:34.969 --> 00:24:37.096
How?

00:24:37.138 --> 00:24:39.436
Fire ants sound vicious.

00:24:39.473 --> 00:24:40.963
Imagine them as your army

00:24:41.008 --> 00:24:43.670
moving in a vast wave
to conquer your enemy.

00:24:43.711 --> 00:24:46.578
There's a massive struggle
going on inside you...

00:24:46.614 --> 00:24:49.515
a battle to the death
between you and the clamp.

00:24:49.550 --> 00:24:52.713
You have to use whatever force
you can to defeat it.

00:24:52.753 --> 00:24:56.416
I'd rather use my energy
to work on getting out of here.

00:25:00.427 --> 00:25:03.885
When I first got here,
I assumed the clamp

00:25:03.931 --> 00:25:06.764
was just a refined form
of torture

00:25:06.800 --> 00:25:10.736
to make our prison stay
that much more arduous.

00:25:10.771 --> 00:25:16.573
Gradually, I began
to understand it more fully.

00:25:16.610 --> 00:25:18.703
It's all right here
in my manifesto...

00:25:18.746 --> 00:25:20.441
my insights, my reasoning...

00:25:22.116 --> 00:25:25.415
...my evidence.

00:25:25.452 --> 00:25:27.579
It's an experiment.

00:25:27.621 --> 00:25:31.421
They're studying us
like animals...

00:25:31.458 --> 00:25:34.916
pitting us against each other
to find out what happens.

00:25:34.962 --> 00:25:36.793
You can see that, can't you?

00:25:38.632 --> 00:25:40.099
I guess so.

00:25:40.134 --> 00:25:42.432
The greatest threat,
of course, would be

00:25:42.469 --> 00:25:43.959
if we started to cooperate
with each other,

00:25:44.004 --> 00:25:47.405
so they prevented that.

00:25:47.441 --> 00:25:49.568
But there had to be
more to it than that,

00:25:49.610 --> 00:25:50.975
and the longer I was in here,

00:25:51.078 --> 00:25:52.978
the more I knew it was my job
to figure it out.

00:25:53.047 --> 00:25:56.642
That's the reason I was put here
and eventually...

00:25:57.985 --> 00:26:00.351
...it came to me

00:26:00.387 --> 00:26:06.383
as though a fireball
had exploded in my mind.

00:26:06.427 --> 00:26:11.729
And the realization gave me
a power over the others.

00:26:11.765 --> 00:26:14.734
They don't come near me anymore.

00:26:14.768 --> 00:26:19.603
They're afraid of me,
because I know the truth.

00:26:22.243 --> 00:26:23.232
Well?

00:26:23.277 --> 00:26:25.939
Don't you want to know
what it is?

00:26:26.013 --> 00:26:29.073
What is the ultimate purpose
of the clamp?

00:26:29.116 --> 00:26:31.107
Okay.

00:26:35.322 --> 00:26:38.758
It's inspired, brilliant.

00:26:38.792 --> 00:26:42.751
It's a method for controlling
the prison population.

00:26:42.796 --> 00:26:45.924
We kill each other off.

00:26:45.966 --> 00:26:48.594
Sure. Whatever you say.

00:26:48.636 --> 00:26:50.536
So you must enter
into the battle.

00:26:50.571 --> 00:26:52.334
If you let the clamp
control you,

00:26:52.373 --> 00:26:54.466
you'll end up
like that crazy old man

00:26:54.508 --> 00:26:55.975
that took over your shelter.

00:26:56.010 --> 00:26:58.979
But if you learn to control it,
you'll survive...

00:26:59.079 --> 00:27:01.070
like me.

00:27:08.921 --> 00:27:10.718
Yes.

00:27:10.756 --> 00:27:15.557
I plan to be out of here
before it even becomes an issue.

00:27:15.594 --> 00:27:17.061
Go ahead.

00:27:17.096 --> 00:27:18.586
Touch it.

00:28:10.583 --> 00:28:12.050
What do you see?

00:28:12.084 --> 00:28:14.075
Some kind of hatch.

00:28:25.097 --> 00:28:27.065
What do you see?

00:28:27.099 --> 00:28:28.999
Are we at the surface?

00:28:54.760 --> 00:28:56.250
Harry.

00:28:57.429 --> 00:28:59.090
How are you feeling?

00:29:02.268 --> 00:29:04.099
I was dreaming...

00:29:05.638 --> 00:29:07.538
about Megan Delaney.

00:29:09.675 --> 00:29:12.508
Next time,
I'll try not to wake you.

00:29:16.348 --> 00:29:18.816
The chute...

00:29:18.851 --> 00:29:20.512
you made it in?

00:29:24.023 --> 00:29:26.014
Did you find a way out?

00:29:29.028 --> 00:29:30.825
Not yet...

00:29:30.863 --> 00:29:32.660
but we're very close.

00:29:32.698 --> 00:29:34.666
It's just a matter of time.

00:29:34.700 --> 00:29:37.362
So you've got
to hang in there, okay?

00:29:51.450 --> 00:29:53.418
Wh... Wha...

00:29:53.452 --> 00:29:54.851
What happened to me?

00:29:54.887 --> 00:29:56.354
Easy, Tom.

00:29:56.388 --> 00:29:58.356
You got stabbed, remember?

00:29:58.390 --> 00:30:01.848
Who... who did it?

00:30:01.894 --> 00:30:03.452
One of the prisoners.

00:30:03.495 --> 00:30:05.360
No, it...

00:30:05.397 --> 00:30:06.762
No, it was you.

00:30:06.799 --> 00:30:09.768
I'm trying
to change your bandage.

00:30:09.802 --> 00:30:10.860
No! Get away from me!

00:30:10.903 --> 00:30:12.871
- Please! I'm trying to help you.
- Get away from me!

00:30:12.905 --> 00:30:14.770
Tom!

00:30:14.807 --> 00:30:16.365
Tom, give me the pipe.

00:30:18.110 --> 00:30:21.409
We need it to get out of here.
Remember?

00:30:22.781 --> 00:30:24.942
It's okay.

00:30:24.984 --> 00:30:27.748
Let me take it.

00:30:45.804 --> 00:30:47.294
Harry...

00:30:51.076 --> 00:30:53.067
...what's happening to me?

00:30:59.084 --> 00:31:01.245
You're gonna be okay.

00:31:08.093 --> 00:31:09.560
Harry.

00:31:09.595 --> 00:31:11.085
Yeah.

00:31:11.130 --> 00:31:14.827
Don't leave me here.

00:31:32.951 --> 00:31:34.942
Close your eyes.

00:32:12.758 --> 00:32:14.419
Sleep well?

00:32:15.594 --> 00:32:16.891
No.

00:32:16.929 --> 00:32:18.226
How about your friend?

00:32:18.263 --> 00:32:20.060
Is he dead yet?

00:32:20.099 --> 00:32:21.589
Shut up!

00:32:29.108 --> 00:32:32.441
The chute leads
to a docking port, right?

00:32:33.612 --> 00:32:36.911
Some kind of ship must come
to drop off food...

00:32:36.949 --> 00:32:38.576
drop off new prisoners.

00:32:38.617 --> 00:32:41.245
So maybe we could
get aboard the ship.

00:32:41.286 --> 00:32:43.254
It's getting the best of you.

00:32:43.288 --> 00:32:44.585
I know we could do it.

00:32:44.623 --> 00:32:46.113
You think they're just
gonna open the hatch

00:32:46.158 --> 00:32:47.455
and ask us if we'd
like a ride home?!

00:32:47.493 --> 00:32:50.189
We'd have
the element of surprise.

00:32:50.229 --> 00:32:52.561
And they'd have the pulse guns.

00:33:00.239 --> 00:33:02.901
If we could hold them off...

00:33:04.243 --> 00:33:05.904
...distract them...

00:33:06.912 --> 00:33:08.743
...just for a few minutes...

00:33:09.915 --> 00:33:12.042
I could
establish our location...

00:33:12.084 --> 00:33:13.551
That's enough!

00:33:13.585 --> 00:33:16.053
...get a message to Voyager

00:33:16.088 --> 00:33:18.716
and they could
get us out of here.

00:33:18.757 --> 00:33:20.384
We'll need weapons.

00:33:20.425 --> 00:33:23.952
I've never
let anyone see this...

00:33:24.029 --> 00:33:27.226
but I'm going to let you read
my manifesto.

00:33:27.266 --> 00:33:30.258
It'll teach you
how to control the clamp.

00:33:32.604 --> 00:33:35.232
I don't want to read
your crazy manifesto.

00:33:35.274 --> 00:33:36.764
Take it.

00:33:36.808 --> 00:33:38.366
Learn everything I know.

00:33:38.410 --> 00:33:41.811
Now, are you going
to help me or not?!

00:33:45.951 --> 00:33:48.112
If I were like the others...

00:33:50.389 --> 00:33:52.050
...l'd kill you.

00:33:53.559 --> 00:33:55.857
But I don't lose control.

00:33:55.894 --> 00:34:00.228
That's the difference
between me and you.

00:34:11.176 --> 00:34:13.406
Listen!
Listen to me, everybody!

00:34:13.445 --> 00:34:14.412
Now what's he want?

00:34:14.446 --> 00:34:15.572
This is important.

00:34:15.614 --> 00:34:17.104
I've got something to say.

00:34:17.149 --> 00:34:19.242
Something you want to hear.

00:34:19.284 --> 00:34:20.911
It's what you've
been waiting for.

00:34:20.953 --> 00:34:22.682
What the hell do you want?

00:34:24.056 --> 00:34:25.751
I've found a way out of here.

00:34:28.560 --> 00:34:30.960
There's no way out.

00:34:31.029 --> 00:34:32.690
There is!

00:34:32.731 --> 00:34:34.221
Through the chute!

00:34:34.266 --> 00:34:35.665
I've been inside.

00:34:37.502 --> 00:34:38.833
Listen!

00:34:38.870 --> 00:34:41.896
We have to work together.

00:34:41.940 --> 00:34:44.568
They'd like us all
to kill each other,

00:34:44.610 --> 00:34:46.908
but we have to cooperate.

00:34:46.945 --> 00:34:49.846
If we do,
we can get out of here.

00:34:49.881 --> 00:34:52.179
If you've been in the chute,

00:34:52.217 --> 00:34:53.878
where does it lead?

00:34:55.220 --> 00:34:56.812
Space.

00:35:01.024 --> 00:35:04.357
It's the truth.

00:35:04.394 --> 00:35:06.055
We can escape...

00:35:07.897 --> 00:35:10.388
...if we work together!

00:35:29.819 --> 00:35:31.810
What the hell are you doing?

00:35:31.854 --> 00:35:34.186
Stay back.

00:35:36.926 --> 00:35:38.416
You've ruined it.

00:35:40.196 --> 00:35:41.663
This is mine.

00:35:41.698 --> 00:35:44.258
It's mine!

00:35:51.874 --> 00:35:54.843
Please! No!

00:35:54.877 --> 00:35:56.071
Please!

00:35:56.112 --> 00:35:57.079
Harry!

00:35:57.113 --> 00:35:58.102
No!

00:36:04.988 --> 00:36:06.853
Go ahead.

00:36:06.889 --> 00:36:08.720
Finish him.

00:36:28.645 --> 00:36:31.045
You wanted to kill him,
didn't you?

00:36:31.080 --> 00:36:32.445
He's my best friend!

00:36:32.482 --> 00:36:34.279
No, no,
that's where you're wrong.

00:36:34.317 --> 00:36:35.909
He's too far gone
to be your friend.

00:36:35.952 --> 00:36:37.579
All he is now is a burden.

00:36:37.620 --> 00:36:38.917
That's not true!

00:36:38.955 --> 00:36:40.889
He eats your food,
he ruined your device...

00:36:40.923 --> 00:36:42.481
he's given in to the clamp.

00:36:42.525 --> 00:36:43.753
You've got to get rid of him

00:36:43.793 --> 00:36:44.953
before he brings you
down with him.

00:36:45.061 --> 00:36:46.790
- Quiet!
- You've got a chance

00:36:46.829 --> 00:36:48.296
to make something
of your life in here,

00:36:48.331 --> 00:36:50.299
but as long as that carcass
is in my hut,

00:36:50.333 --> 00:36:54.201
we'll never be able to go on
to more important things.

00:36:54.237 --> 00:36:56.535
What the hell are
you talking about?

00:36:56.572 --> 00:36:59.200
We've got to disseminate
the manifesto...

00:36:59.242 --> 00:37:01.540
gather our followers...

00:37:01.577 --> 00:37:03.067
train them.

00:37:04.914 --> 00:37:06.211
You're insane.

00:37:06.249 --> 00:37:07.546
You want my protection?

00:37:07.583 --> 00:37:09.551
You want to live under my roof?

00:37:09.585 --> 00:37:10.882
Get rid of him.

00:37:10.920 --> 00:37:12.581
I don't need your protection!

00:37:15.258 --> 00:37:17.556
How long do you
think you'll last

00:37:17.593 --> 00:37:19.220
against Pit and the others,

00:37:19.262 --> 00:37:21.253
without me looking out for you?

00:37:25.268 --> 00:37:27.236
Go ahead. Take it.

00:37:27.270 --> 00:37:29.898
Think of what
a relief it will be

00:37:29.939 --> 00:37:31.907
to not have
that responsibility...

00:37:31.941 --> 00:37:34.432
to be free of his ranting.

00:37:55.231 --> 00:37:57.426
I'm not a killer.

00:37:57.467 --> 00:37:59.867
If you want
to survive in here...

00:37:59.902 --> 00:38:01.597
you'd better learn to be.

00:38:01.637 --> 00:38:06.233
If that's what it takes
to stay alive...

00:38:10.246 --> 00:38:12.237
then I'd rather die.

00:38:14.584 --> 00:38:16.245
Get out now.

00:38:18.087 --> 00:38:19.918
And take him with you...

00:38:21.424 --> 00:38:23.221
...or I will kill him.

00:38:28.765 --> 00:38:31.233
Unless you've decided
to relinquish control

00:38:31.267 --> 00:38:32.666
of your vessel, Captain,

00:38:32.702 --> 00:38:36.536
I suggest that you do not
proceed across our border.

00:38:36.572 --> 00:38:38.130
We've captured the ship and crew

00:38:38.174 --> 00:38:40.699
responsible for the bombing
at the Laktivia canteen.

00:38:40.743 --> 00:38:42.210
I see.

00:38:42.245 --> 00:38:43.735
I'm prepared to trade them

00:38:43.780 --> 00:38:45.941
for the immediate
and unconditional release

00:38:46.015 --> 00:38:47.880
of Lieutenant Paris
and Ensign Kim.

00:38:47.917 --> 00:38:51.216
Your crewmen have already
been tried and convicted.

00:38:51.254 --> 00:38:54.382
Are you saying those
convictions can't be reversed,

00:38:54.423 --> 00:38:57.620
no matter what new evidence
is brought to light?

00:38:57.660 --> 00:38:59.127
You are correct.

00:38:59.162 --> 00:39:01.460
That is an outrageous policy.

00:39:01.497 --> 00:39:05.797
I assure you, it has proved to
be a most effective deterrent.

00:39:05.835 --> 00:39:08.167
Good day, Captain.

00:39:09.705 --> 00:39:11.866
So much for negotiating.

00:39:11.908 --> 00:39:14.706
What should we do
with the prisoners?

00:39:14.744 --> 00:39:17.269
Bring Vel to my ready room.
Now.

00:39:19.682 --> 00:39:21.582
I want the location
and shield code

00:39:21.617 --> 00:39:23.915
to the maximum security
detention facility.

00:39:23.953 --> 00:39:25.147
What's wrong,

00:39:25.188 --> 00:39:28.351
the Akritirians didn't
agree to your terms?

00:39:28.391 --> 00:39:30.689
No, as a matter of fact.

00:39:30.726 --> 00:39:32.694
But I suspect you will.

00:39:32.728 --> 00:39:35.526
And what makes you so sure?

00:39:35.565 --> 00:39:37.897
Because if you don't,
you and your sister

00:39:37.934 --> 00:39:40.994
are going to spend the rest
of your lives in prison.

00:39:46.042 --> 00:39:48.943
I'll take you to the prison

00:39:49.011 --> 00:39:52.777
and I'll get you in,

00:39:52.815 --> 00:39:55.477
but there are members
of Open Sky in there

00:39:55.518 --> 00:39:57.645
and I want to get them out, too.

00:39:57.687 --> 00:40:00.349
I don't think you understand
the way this works.

00:40:00.389 --> 00:40:02.152
You tell me what I want to know,

00:40:02.191 --> 00:40:05.718
and after I get my people back,
I let you and your sister go.

00:40:05.761 --> 00:40:07.956
That's not good enough.

00:40:08.030 --> 00:40:11.261
Mr. Tuvok,
inform the Akritirians

00:40:11.300 --> 00:40:13.495
that we're ready
to turn the prisoners over.

00:40:15.838 --> 00:40:16.964
All right.

00:40:17.073 --> 00:40:21.737
Crewman Foster, take the
prisoner to Commander Chakotay.

00:40:21.777 --> 00:40:24.405
He will upload
the coordinates and codes.

00:40:27.984 --> 00:40:29.611
May I ask how you propose

00:40:29.652 --> 00:40:31.813
to get past
the Akritirian patrols?

00:40:31.854 --> 00:40:33.412
No doubt they will attack

00:40:33.456 --> 00:40:35.856
as soon as Voyager
crosses the border.

00:40:35.892 --> 00:40:39.089
That's exactly why the rescue
team won't be aboard Voyager.

00:40:39.128 --> 00:40:41.153
Captain?

00:40:41.197 --> 00:40:43.358
If I'm not mistaken,

00:40:43.399 --> 00:40:46.664
Mr. Neelix's ship
is still in our shuttle bay.

00:40:46.702 --> 00:40:49.000
Yes.
However, Mr. Neelix's vessel

00:40:49.071 --> 00:40:52.006
has extremely limited
combat capabilities.

00:40:53.209 --> 00:40:55.700
Then we'll have to be
very careful, won't we?

00:41:00.883 --> 00:41:04.944
I want his clothes
and I want his shoes!

00:41:05.054 --> 00:41:06.885
This man is my friend.

00:41:06.923 --> 00:41:09.357
Nobody touches him.

00:41:09.392 --> 00:41:12.589
Back off!
You won't have to get hurt.

00:41:16.565 --> 00:41:18.192
New prisoner!

00:41:29.111 --> 00:41:30.100
I got her!

00:41:31.647 --> 00:41:32.841
Hands on your heads.

00:41:32.882 --> 00:41:33.940
Do it now!

00:41:33.983 --> 00:41:35.473
Neelix to Lieutenant Tuvok.

00:41:35.518 --> 00:41:36.678
Go ahead.

00:41:36.719 --> 00:41:38.209
We've got company.

00:41:38.254 --> 00:41:40.814
Two Akritirian patrol ships
on an intercept course.

00:41:40.856 --> 00:41:42.949
I'm not sure how long
I can hold them off.

00:41:42.992 --> 00:41:45.290
We are moving as quickly
as we can, Mr. Neelix.

00:41:45.328 --> 00:41:46.727
Captain!

00:41:47.730 --> 00:41:49.254
Where's Tom?

00:41:49.298 --> 00:41:51.027
He needs help.

00:41:55.171 --> 00:41:57.731
Akritirian patrol
to alien vessel.

00:41:57.773 --> 00:41:59.502
Disengage immediately.

00:41:59.542 --> 00:42:00.907
Akritirian patrol?

00:42:00.943 --> 00:42:03.241
Uh, am I in Akritirian space?

00:42:03.279 --> 00:42:04.610
Oh, dear.

00:42:04.647 --> 00:42:07.946
I thought this was
the Heva Vll refueling port.

00:42:07.984 --> 00:42:09.781
Uh, you wouldn't, by any chance,

00:42:09.819 --> 00:42:13.186
be able to recommend a...
respectable establishment

00:42:13.222 --> 00:42:16.623
where I could have
my navigational array repaired?

00:42:16.659 --> 00:42:17.921
Disengage immediately.

00:42:17.960 --> 00:42:19.552
This is your final warning.

00:42:19.595 --> 00:42:20.619
Janeway to Neelix.

00:42:20.663 --> 00:42:21.721
Everyone's aboard.

00:42:21.764 --> 00:42:22.924
Acknowledged.

00:42:22.965 --> 00:42:25.058
I know it's a little
cramped back there,

00:42:25.101 --> 00:42:27.797
so if there's anything I can do
to make you more comfortable...

00:42:27.837 --> 00:42:29.964
Neelix!
Just get us out of here!

00:42:30.006 --> 00:42:32.236
Of course, Captain.

00:42:32.274 --> 00:42:35.243
Talaxian vessel
to Akritirian patrol.

00:42:35.277 --> 00:42:36.972
My apologies
for the little mix-up.

00:42:37.079 --> 00:42:39.445
I'll be departing now,
per your orders.

00:42:48.891 --> 00:42:51.985
Power down your engines
and prepare to be boarded.

00:42:52.094 --> 00:42:53.220
Eh, what was that, patrol?

00:42:53.262 --> 00:42:54.889
That last message was garbled.

00:43:03.005 --> 00:43:05.769
I've always thought
of my piloting skills

00:43:05.808 --> 00:43:06.934
as modest, at best,

00:43:07.009 --> 00:43:09.944
and the conditions
were extremely dangerous.

00:43:10.012 --> 00:43:13.607
Still, I did outmaneuver
those Akritirians, didn't I?

00:43:13.649 --> 00:43:15.742
You did a terrific job, Neelix.

00:43:15.785 --> 00:43:16.911
I agree.

00:43:16.952 --> 00:43:18.317
Excellent piloting.

00:43:18.354 --> 00:43:19.946
I'm glad to hear you
say that, Captain,

00:43:20.022 --> 00:43:21.512
because I've been thinking...

00:43:21.557 --> 00:43:23.252
until Tom here
gets back on his feet,

00:43:23.292 --> 00:43:27.490
perhaps I could try my hand
at conn for a while.

00:43:27.530 --> 00:43:28.963
That won't be necessary.

00:43:29.065 --> 00:43:32.296
Lieutenant Paris is just fine,
thanks to excellent doctoring.

00:43:32.334 --> 00:43:33.631
I finished analyzing
these implants,

00:43:33.669 --> 00:43:35.364
and you'll be happy to
know that the treatment

00:43:35.404 --> 00:43:37.804
I provided will successfully
counteract their effect on you.

00:43:37.840 --> 00:43:39.330
What exactly was the effect?

00:43:39.375 --> 00:43:40.842
My readings indicate
that the implants

00:43:40.876 --> 00:43:42.309
are designed
to stimulate the production

00:43:42.344 --> 00:43:44.107
of acetylcholine
in the hypothalamus.

00:43:44.146 --> 00:43:45.704
That would explain
the agitation.

00:43:45.748 --> 00:43:48.080
Hmm. Acetylcholine
is a brain chemical

00:43:48.117 --> 00:43:51.314
common to the neural
structures of most humanoids.

00:43:51.353 --> 00:43:55.255
Essentially, it helps stimulate
one's aggressive tendencies.

00:43:55.291 --> 00:43:57.691
Zio was right.

00:44:00.196 --> 00:44:01.925
Come on, Harry.

00:44:01.997 --> 00:44:03.589
We're overdue
for that steak dinner.

00:44:03.632 --> 00:44:05.759
I guess so.

00:44:05.801 --> 00:44:08.429
What do you mean,
"Guess so"?

00:44:08.471 --> 00:44:09.597
It's the thought of that dinner

00:44:09.638 --> 00:44:10.696
that kept us going.

00:44:10.739 --> 00:44:12.229
So... what do you think?

00:44:12.274 --> 00:44:13.673
Uh, a baked potato...

00:44:13.709 --> 00:44:16.234
a big mound
of deep-fried onion rings?

00:44:16.278 --> 00:44:17.472
Tom...

00:44:17.513 --> 00:44:20.073
Maybe, maybe, uh...
some grilled mushrooms.

00:44:20.116 --> 00:44:21.777
Tom, listen to me.

00:44:21.817 --> 00:44:23.808
I...

00:44:25.121 --> 00:44:27.055
I almost killed you.

00:44:27.089 --> 00:44:28.351
What are you saying?

00:44:28.390 --> 00:44:29.618
You're the one
that kept me alive.

00:44:29.658 --> 00:44:31.956
I was ready to hit
you with the pipe.

00:44:32.061 --> 00:44:33.392
Don't you remember?

00:44:35.331 --> 00:44:38.562
You want to know
what I remember?

00:44:38.601 --> 00:44:41.627
Someone saying,
"This man is my friend.

00:44:41.670 --> 00:44:44.468
Nobody touches him."

00:44:44.507 --> 00:44:47.601
I'll remember that
for a long time.

00:44:49.612 --> 00:44:51.102
So...

00:44:51.147 --> 00:44:52.637
what do you say we blow

00:44:52.681 --> 00:44:55.081
a week's worth
of replicator rations?

00:44:56.285 --> 00:44:57.809
So, what's for dessert?

00:44:57.853 --> 00:44:59.912
Cherry pie, don't you remember?

00:44:59.955 --> 00:45:02.321
What about the fudge
ripple pudding?

00:45:02.358 --> 00:45:04.349
Ah! Yes...
